<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wube Haile Maryam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wube Haile Maryam was the lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semien">Semien</a> who also ruled Tigray from 1831 to 1855, making him one of the strongest regional rulers of the Ethiopian Era of Princes. He sought European contacts and firearms to strengthen his position. Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosice">Kassa</a> Hailu at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-deresge">Battle of Deresge</a> in 1855, he was imprisoned by Kassa, now Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tewodros-ii">Tewodros II</a>, and spent the rest of his life in captivity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wube-haile-maryam.jpg" alt="Wube Haile Maryam" width="320" height="512" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alphonse-Marie-Adolphe de Neuville · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ras_Wub%C3%A9_of_Tigre.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
